        "id": "two-source-pendulum-panels",
        "description": "Source panel a has a stand, vertical string and bob, upward vector F0 and downward vector G at equilibrium. Source panel b shows the SAME pendulum with three equal-string-length positions: left solid and bottom/right ghost positions; dashed vertical and right strings, a dashed curved trajectory and opposed horizontal motion arrows. Preserve both a/b panels, including unchanged string length across the equilibrium and moving states. Symmetric endpoints and exact constant string length are justified modern schematic regularization of an unmeasured source drawing, not queried data. Hollow ghost bobs replace source stippling without changing their alternative-position meaning. Small pivot and bob-center markers are modern construction aids for the fixed-length relationship, not additional source particles.",
